# EtOtpInput Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtOtpInput` is a compound component for OTP / PIN code entry in the eToro design system. It provides:

- **Configurable length**: 2–9 character slots
- **Cell sizes (`OtpInputSize`)**: `large` \| `medium` \| `small` — auto from `length`, or optional `size` override
- **Show/hide toggle**: Optional `EtOtpInput.Toggle` subcomponent for secure entry
- **Error message**: Optional `EtOtpInput.ErrorMessage` subcomponent for displaying error text below cells
- **Built-in states**: focus, error, disabled, secure entry
- **Hidden TextInput**: A single invisible `TextInput` handles keyboard input; visual cells are rendered on top
- **iOS SMS autofill**: Uses `textContentType="oneTimeCode"` and `autoComplete="one-time-code"`
- **Controlled & uncontrolled modes**: Supports `value` (controlled) and `defaultValue` (uncontrolled)

**Does NOT handle:**

- Form validation logic (handle in parent)
- Resend code / timer logic (handle in parent)
- Navigation after completion (handle via `onComplete` callback)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtOtpInput` (root component)

```tsx
<EtOtpInput
  length={6}                              // Required: 2–9 characters
  value?: string                          // Controlled mode
  defaultValue?: string                   // Uncontrolled mode
  onChangeText?: (text: string) => void   // Fires on every character change
  onComplete?: (code: string) => void     // Fires when all cells are filled
  error?: boolean                         // Error state (red styling)
  disabled?: boolean                      // Prevents input
  secureEntry?: boolean                   // Show dots instead of digits
  autoFocus?: boolean                     // Focus on mount (default: false)
  haptics?: boolean                       // Haptic feedback (default: true)
  keyboardType?: KeyboardTypeOptions      // Default: 'number-pad'
  size?: 'large' | 'medium' | 'small'     // Optional; default from length
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
>
  {children}   {/* Optional: EtOtpInput.Toggle, EtOtpInput.ErrorMessage */}
</EtOtpInput>
```

### Size (default from length, optional override)

Default cell size follows `length` (same as always). Pass `size` only when you need a tier that does not match length (e.g. Storybook / dev previews).

| Length | `OtpInputSize` | Cell Width | Cell Height | TextVariant     | Dot Size  |
| ------ | -------------- | ---------- | ----------- | --------------- | --------- |
| 2–3    | `large`        | X15 (60px) | X17 (68px)  | `num-xl-medium` | X4 (16px) |
| 4–6    | `medium`       | X12 (48px) | X13 (52px)  | `num-l-medium`  | X3 (12px) |
| 7–9    | `small`        | X8 (32px)  | X13 (52px)  | `num-ml-medium` | X3 (12px) |

Gap between cells is X1 (4px) for all sizes.

### `EtOtpInput.Toggle`

```tsx
<EtOtpInput.Toggle
  accessibilityLabel?: string   // Custom label (defaults to 'Show code' / 'Hide code')
  testID?: string
/>
```

- Must be used inside `<EtOtpInput>`.
- Reads and toggles `isSecure` state from context.
- Renders `eye` / `eye-slash` icon via `EtIconV2`.

### `EtOtpInput.ErrorMessage`

```tsx
<EtOtpInput.ErrorMessage
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
>
  {children}   // Error message text (ReactNode)
</EtOtpInput.ErrorMessage>
```

- Must be used inside `<EtOtpInput>`.
- Renders below the OTP cells (automatically separated from the cell row via child filtering).
- Uses `colors.actionBrandVarText` (red) for error text color.
- Uses `EtText` with `body-tiny-regular` variant.
- Has `accessibilityRole="alert"` (iOS VoiceOver) and `accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"` (Android TalkBack) for screen reader announcement.
- Consumer controls visibility — wrap in a conditional to show/hide.

## Usage Patterns

### Basic OTP (6-digit, auto `medium`)

```tsx
<EtOtpInput length={6} onComplete={handleComplete} />
```

### Short PIN (3-digit, auto `large`)

```tsx
<EtOtpInput length={3} onComplete={handleComplete} />
```

### Long code with toggle (8-digit, auto `small`)

```tsx
<EtOtpInput length={8} secureEntry onComplete={handleComplete}>
  <EtOtpInput.Toggle />
</EtOtpInput>
```

### Error state, controlled

```tsx
<EtOtpInput length={4} value={otp} onChangeText={setOtp} error onComplete={handleComplete}>
  <EtOtpInput.Toggle />
</EtOtpInput>
```

### Error state with error message

```tsx
<EtOtpInput length={6} error onComplete={handleComplete}>
  <EtOtpInput.Toggle />
  <EtOtpInput.ErrorMessage>Invalid verification code</EtOtpInput.ErrorMessage>
</EtOtpInput>
```

### Conditional error message (consumer-controlled)

```tsx
<EtOtpInput length={6} error={hasError} onComplete={handleComplete}>
  {hasError && <EtOtpInput.ErrorMessage>The code you entered is incorrect</EtOtpInput.ErrorMessage>}
</EtOtpInput>
```

### Disabled

```tsx
<EtOtpInput length={6} disabled defaultValue="123456" />
```

## Anti-patterns

### Using Toggle outside EtOtpInput

```tsx
// BAD — will throw a runtime error
<EtOtpInput.Toggle />
```

**Fix:** Always wrap inside `<EtOtpInput>`.

### Providing both value and defaultValue

```tsx
// BAD — conflicting controlled/uncontrolled
<EtOtpInput length={4} value={otp} defaultValue="1234" />
```

**Fix:** Use only `value` (controlled) or `defaultValue` (uncontrolled), not both.

## Architecture

### Hidden TextInput Technique

A single hidden `TextInput` (opacity 0, 1x1px) captures all keyboard input. Tapping the visible cell row focuses this hidden input. Each visual cell reads its character from the current value string.

### Context

Single `OtpContext` shares all state with subcomponents:

| Field          | Type                             | Description                    |
| -------------- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| `value`        | `string`                         | Current input value            |
| `isFocused`    | `boolean`                        | Whether hidden input has focus |
| `isSecure`     | `boolean`                        | Whether to show dots           |
| `error`        | `boolean`                        | Error state                    |
| `disabled`     | `boolean`                        | Disabled state                 |
| `size`         | `'large' \| 'medium' \| 'small'` | Resolved tier (from `length` or `size` prop) |
| `length`       | `number`                         | Number of cells                |
| `toggleSecure` | `() => void`                     | Toggle show/hide               |

No split context needed — OTP updates are bounded (max 9 chars), re-renders are cheap.

### Hooks

- **`useOtpConfig`**: Props + theme → resolved cell config (dimensions, colors, typography). Pure computation, `useMemo`-wrapped.
- **`useOtpState`**: Manages internal state (value, focus, secure toggle, TextInput ref). Returns state + handlers.
- **Digit typography**: `small` → `num-ml-medium`, `medium` → `num-l-medium`, `large` → `num-xl-medium` (Figma Num ML/L/XL at medium weight).

- **`getOtpSize`**: Pure function that maps length → `large` / `medium` / `small`.

### Input behavior

- **Digits only**: `onChangeText` output is stripped to `[0-9]` and clamped to `length` (paste-safe).
- **Focus**: tapping the cell row focuses the hidden input; the active cell is always the **next empty** slot (`min(value.length, length - 1)`), sequential entry only.

### Cell Styling (Figma phone digits)

- **Default / filled / focused active slot**: same fill — `colors.bgNeutralGreyPrimary`
- **Active cell** (focused caret slot): `1px` `colors.dividerPrimary` only (or error color when `error`); background unchanged
- **Border**: only on the active cell when the hidden input is focused; `borderWidth` 0 otherwise
- **Radii**: `small` / `medium` → X2 (8px); `large` → ~9.5px

## Dependencies

### Internal

- `useEtoroTheme` — theme colors
- `EtText` — digit text rendering
- `EtIconV2` — eye/eye-slash icons in Toggle
- Spacing constants (`X1`, `X2`, `X3`, `X4`, `X8`, `X12`, `X13`, `X15`, `X17`)

### External

- `expo-haptics` — haptic feedback on focus and toggle
- `react-native` — `TextInput`, `View`, `Pressable`, `StyleSheet`

